## Stage 1 (preprocessing + internal process)

### Type 1 preprocessing (8 steps)
Journey detection â†’ sanity check (gate) â†’ initial intent capture â†’ slug+display name â†’ intent deepening dialog (problem/users/non-goals/success) â†’ preferences dialog (likes/dislikes/must_haves/avoid + optional hints) â†’ AI sketches (features/flows/risks) â†’ trigger + ND1 finalize.

### T2P (13 steps)
Same common pattern + F1/F2/F3/F4 processing per artifact. Each artifact gets an MCQ: overhaul / keep-as-is / selective-tweak / discard / identify-likes. Pre-populates intent + preferences from artifact analysis.

### Stage 1 internal process (11 sub-steps)
Read ND1 â†’ carryover application â†’ produce 7 SO1 docs in order (Doc 1, 3, 2, 4, 5, 7, 8) â†’ 5-pass VERIFICATION (format / mandatory / cross-doc / consistency / interconnection) â†’ handoff.

### Carryover rules (ND1 â†’ SO1)
- intent fields â†’ Doc 1 manifest
- likes/dislikes/must_haves/avoid â†’ Doc 1 `preferences` block (NEW field, Doc 1 grows to 14 components)
- ui_hints â†’ Doc 4 component-shortlist preferences
- tech_hints â†’ Doc 8 staging ADR
- integrations_initial â†’ Doc 7 third_party_services seed
- auth_intent â†’ Doc 7 auth_strategy seed
- inspirations â†’ central UI asset repo + project preferences
- F1-F4 â†’ source files moved to repo + decisions in staging ADR
- features/flows/risks_concerns sketches â†’ refined into final SO1

---

## Stage 2 (UI + Tech finalization)

### 8 sub-stages
Input validation â†’ UI Master Plan (locked theme, palette, fonts, animation, aspect ratios) â†’ pages walkthrough â†’ master components list build (cross-project scan) â†’ component-by-component selection (â‰¥2-3 options per component, user picks) â†’ tech stack + architecture (Mermaid diagrams) â†’ build plan â†’ verification.

### UI Master Plan requirements
- Aspect ratios: desktop / mobile / tablet / both (default both)
- Dark + light modes (mandatory both, no single-mode sites)
- Min 3 accent colors per palette
- 27" desktop + mobile browser support
- Fonts: heading + body + monospace (configurable; Outfit + JetBrains Mono is house default)
- Animation level: none / subtle / smooth / playful
- Spacing/shadow/radius/iconography systems

### Master Components List (cross-project asset library)
Scan all `/mnt/storage/websites/*` â†’ extract components â†’ categorize â†’ cross-reference asset library â†’ identify gaps â†’ seed `master_components` table. 15 entries seeded from real cross-project usage.

### Tech stack defaults
Next.js + Tailwind + better-sqlite3 + drizzle (matches user's ecosystem). Override allowed but defaults set.

### Architecture diagrams via Mermaid (free, text-based)

---

## Stage 3 (Build + Test)

### 7 sub-stages with verifier
Scaffolding â†’ pipeline setup â†’ code gen â†’ **VERIFIER SUB-AGENT (mandatory anti-gaslighting)** â†’ multi-tier testing â†’ auto-fix loop â†’ verification & deploy.

### Testing tiers
**Always-run** (every push): Unit (Vitest), Component (Playwright), E2E flows (Playwright), Visual regression (Lost Pixel), a11y (axe).
**First-time + nightly**: Lighthouse perf, Load tests (k6), Security scan (Trivy / Grype / OSV-Scanner â€” NOT Snyk per Codex P1 #11).

### Auto-fix loop
3 iterations max per failure. Stub-detected â†’ bypass auto-fix, escalate to user.

### Per-feature acceptance criteria as test target
"Use case met or not" = atomic done metric. Tests written FROM acceptance criteria. Anti-gaslighting bedrock.

---

## Stage 4 (Iterate â€” the user-testing loop)

### 8 sub-stages with lock-in gate at 4.3
Intake â†’ classify â†’ **ðŸ†• PROPOSE & CONFIRM (LOCK-IN GATE)** â†’ route per item â†’ mini-staging (if needed) â†’ mini-build â†’ verifier per item â†’ integrate + trace report.

### Inputs accepted
- Tracker per-flow bug reports
- Tracker project-level mega-prompts
- Direct chat with Claude
- (future) Auto-feedback from runtime monitoring

### Item types
bug / new_feature_request / feature_modification / flow_modification / page_modification / component_modification / risk_addition / re_wire / revamp / observation / question

### Manual classify trigger
Reports stay `status=pending` until user clicks "Analyze". Saves cost on noise.

### Trace report (the payoff)
Per iteration shows: original raw text â†’ extracted items â†’ built per item (file changes, tests run, verifier verdict) â†’ acceptance criteria regression check â†’ ADR if significant.

### User can keep track of "what I asked vs what got built"
This is THE design driver. Without it, user can't trust the system.

